<title>USA: Fidelity National Q3 loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Fidelity National Q3 loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>For the quarter Ending</p>
<p>							Sep 96	 Sep 95</p>
<p> Total interest income		    15,644,162   12,321,920</p>
<p> Total interest expense		    7,150,652    5,018,316</p>
<p> Net interest income			 8,493,510    7,303,604</p>
<p> Total other expense			 9,521,554    6,457,565</p>
<p> Net income				 ( 1,604,331)    1,236,165</p>
<p> Earnings per share			     (0.35)	   0.27</p>
<p>							  Year to Date</p>
<p>							Sep 96	 Sep 95</p>
<p> Total interest income		    44,325,490   34,897,303</p>
<p> Total interest expense		   19,764,023   13,690,009</p>
<p> Net interest income			24,561,467   21,207,294</p>
<p> Total other income			 12,612,005    7,691,873</p>
<p> Net income					  3,601    3,398,506</p>
<p> Earnings per share				 0.00	   0.74</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610  </p>
<p>NOTE: Full name is Fidelity National Corp.</p>
<p>The company attributed losses for the 1996 quarter to increased credit card charge-offs, which led to increasing the provision for loan losses to $5.7 million vs $2 million.</p>
<p>It also cited a one-time insurance assessment charge, and increased operating costs due to the expansion of the branch network and staff.</p>
